Switch + Pattern Matching (Java 17+ / 21)


Object obj = "Java";

String result = switch (obj) {
    case Integer i -> "Integer: " + i;
    case String s -> "String: " + s;
    case null -> "Null value";
    default -> "Unknown type";
};


Multiple Case Labels (Very common in real code)


int score = 85;

String grade = switch (score / 10) {
    case 9, 10 -> "A";
    case 8 -> "B";
    case 7 -> "C";
    case 6 -> "D";
    default -> "Fail";
};

